# virt32 - QEMU -M virt, 32-bit RISC-V (RV32)
#
# The riscv32 analogue of os/inferno/virt (riscv64): same QEMU virt
# machine, same memory map (verified separately via this host's own
# qemu-system-riscv32 -machine dumpdtb, not assumed from the riscv64
# board), but a completely different kernel toolchain -- zc/za/zl
# (thechar z, Richard Miller's original Plan 9 RISC-V compiler), not
# jc/ja/jl.  za has no CSR read/write operand form and no F-register
# file at all; see virt32/l.s for what that required.
#
# The console path is proven, so this is the first widening past it:
# ether and ip, over the same virtio-mmio NIC riscv64/virt uses.  Still
# no screen (memlayer/memdraw/draw), no SD, no virtio input, no PCI --
# QEMU's riscv32 virt has an ECAM host but nothing this board needs
# behind it yet -- and no entropy device (virt's own board comment:
# randomvirt wants a libsec newer than the one this tree shares).

